peer effects may help explain what motivates workers in jobs with fixed pay.




Strong evidence of productivity spillovers. Substituting a worker with below averagepermanent productivity with a worker with above average permanent productivity is associatedwith a 1 percent increase in the effort of other workers on the same shift. The finding of apositive spillover suggests that positive peer effects dominate free-riding.
